    <briefdescription>
<para>A transition that grows item values from a baseline. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>As an <computeroutput>enterTransition</computeroutput>, the added items grow from <computeroutput>baseline</computeroutput> to their values; as an <computeroutput>exitTransition</computeroutput>, the removed items shrink back to it. Only values grow; positions stay:</para>
<para><table rows="4" cols="2"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Series  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Grows  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1LineCurve" kindref="compound">LineCurve</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1PointCloud" kindref="compound">PointCloud</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Y  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1BarSeries" kindref="compound">BarSeries</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>The bar value  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1ErrorBarSeries" kindref="compound">ErrorBarSeries</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>The center and both bounds  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>With <computeroutput>stagger</computeroutput>, the items grow one after another in a wave.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1DrawTransition" kindref="compound">DrawTransition</ref>, <ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1MorphTransition" kindref="compound">MorphTransition</ref>, <ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1EnterExitTransition" kindref="compound">EnterExitTransition</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
